  "facts": [
    "The Hartland Covered Bridge, opened May 14, 1901, stretches 1,282 feet, making it the longest covered bridge worldwide, a record it still proudly holds today.",
    "After a 1920 freshet collapsed two spans, the bridge was rebuilt as a covered structure in 1921, adding a roof that year and preserving its historic charm for future generations.",
    "Designated a National Historic Site in 1977, the bridge survived a 1970 truck ban, a 2006 guitar contribution, and a 2023 structural survey that temporarily closed it for repairs."
